<title>BELGIUM: Belgium liquidity climbs at money tender.</title>
<headline>Belgium liquidity climbs at money tender.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian National Bank said liquidity climbed at its fixed-rate tender for seven-day advances. Details -</p>
<p>    Value date 06/11	  expiry on 13/11    NBVA</p>
<p>    Amount allotted	   13.600 bln bfr    (12.525 bln *)</p>
<p>    Interest rate	     3.00 pct	    (3.00 pct **)</p>
<p>    Total amount of bids    13.600 bln bfr</p>
<p>Percentage of bids accepted  100</p>
<p>* amount draining from the money market on Wednesday.</p>
<p>** interest rate at previous tender on October 28.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
